# Live empty-compose corpus - tests/harness/check_live_empty_compose.sh
#
# Per row one headless capture of the guest reference at the og VBL and,
# per tick scale and repeat, one windowed eager replay to the frame limit
# that dumps the present of the empty scene at the dump frame; the dump is
# compared with the reference, and the hold census must count no lost
# empty compose.
#
#   <bk2> | <frame-limit> | <dump frame> | <og VBL> | <launch tokens>
#
# `launch` takes the presentation-corpus convention: a whitespace-separated
# token spelled KEY=VALUE with an upper-case key is an environment entry,
# every other token a command-line argument.
#
# start-new-game: scene frame 412 (VBL 985) is empty; the game then
# ClearImages both display buffers, after the scene's ring slot took its
# verdict and before the present thread composes it. The reference is
# black; the VRAM framebuffer still holds the boot logo upload.
start-new-game.bk2 | 1046 | 412 | 985 | --aspect 4:3 --lod original
